  "verdict": "IRRESOLVABLE_BY_STATIC_NULL",
  "verdict_reasons": [
    "FIDELITY FAILS AGAIN, AND THIS TIME IT IS INFORMATIVE. The null's cross-sectional correlation shape is no longer an assumption -- it IS the real in-sample residual correlation matrix, exactly, and the self-check confirms R(1) == R_hat to machine precision. Its in-sample-minus-PIT gap is -0.0989 against the real +2.0457 (error 2.1446 > tolerance 1.0); the best gap ANY rung of either ladder achieves is +0.0452. Since the shape is now correct by construction, the residual mismatch cannot be a shape-calibration problem. It is a DYNAMICS problem: the real factor loadings move over the sample, and a null whose loadings are constant cannot reproduce that no matter how its cross-section is calibrated.",
    "PART A CONFIRMS THAT DIRECTLY, WITHOUT ANY NULL INVERSION: the real top-6 eigenvector subspace rotates 31.88 degrees (largest principal angle) between the first and last walk-forward refit, while constant-loading synthetic panels put the same statistic at 13.84 degrees on average and never above 18.49 across 12 draws. The real loadings genuinely drift; the excess is not sampling noise."
  ],
  "floor": 15.0,
  "judgment_calls": {
    "L1_gaussian_iid": "Gaussian i.i.d.-in-time innovations, matching K2 of the prior script for comparability. Real returns are fat-tailed and vol-clustered.",
    "L2_ladder_and_seeds": "B_true ladder [24.0, 22.0, 20.0, 19.0, 17.0, 15.0, 13.0, 11.0], 40 Monte-Carlo draws per rung, 12 draws for the constant-truth drift baseline. Ordinary choices, not from any source.",
    "L3_empirical_shape_family": "R(g) = normalize(V diag(lambda**g) V') built from the REAL in-sample residual correlation matrix. This script's own construction, not quoted from a paper. Chosen because it holds the empirical eigenvector shape EXACTLY fixed while moving breadth; R(1) == R_hat is machine-checked.",
    "L4_degeneracy_epsilon": "R_hat is exactly rank-deficient: removing k=6 factors leaves 6 zero eigenvalues and rank 25 of 31 (measured, not assumed). The headline ladder keeps that degeneracy; a variant floors the zeros at eps=0.001 to test whether the exact rank deficiency drives the result. Both reported.",
    "L5_fidelity_tolerance": "Null must land within 1.0 of the real in-sample-minus-PIT gap of +2.0457. PRE-DECLARED, and identical to the threshold the prior merged script used, so this attempt is not graded on a softer curve.",
    "L6_principal_angles": "Drift measured by principal angles between top-k eigenvector SUBSPACES (Bjorck & Golub 1973, SVD formulation), not raw eigenvector comparison, because eigenvectors carry arbitrary sign and can swap order when eigenvalues are close -- both of which would manufacture fake drift. Routine self-checked against four cases with known answers.",
    "L7_inherited": "burn_in=504, refit_every=21, correlation PCA, k=6 held fixed at the merged report's values; changing them would break comparability with 16.9550."
